# Unity tooling safety

Authoritative: [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), [docs/05-qa-plan.md](../../docs/05-qa-plan.md).  
Studio contract (when available): Production OS `docs/unity-tooling.md`.

Unity CLI, Pipeline, and MCP are **optional**. Prefer a backend only when the **needed capability** is verified for this exact project. Do not select CLI merely because a `unity` binary exists. Do not silently fall back to another backend for mutations.

If tooling is disconnected or identity unverifiable: no Editor mutations; continue with code/docs/tests; report identity **unverified**.

## Before any mutation — exact identity

1. Canonicalize **repo / project root** (absolute path; resolve symlinks).
2. Canonicalize the tooling-reported project path (CLI `projectPath`, MCP `GetProjectRoot`, or equivalent).
3. **Require exact string equality.** Refuse mutation if they differ or either cannot be verified.
4. Do not use name/suffix heuristics or hardcoded user home paths.
5. Confirm **active scene** or target asset matches the task.
6. Prefer a clean git checkpoint or document pre-existing dirty state.
7. One writable Editor session — do not race another agent on the same scene/prefab.

## Permission levels

- **READ** — status, inspect scene/console, safe captures, capability detection.
- **CONTROLLED_WRITE** — approved named commands within explicit scope (task-bound).
- **ARBITRARY_EXECUTION** — eval, unrestricted C#, package ops, arbitrary scripts — **separate explicit approval**.

## Allowed without special approval

Read-only inspect: project data, console, hierarchy, package **get**, editor get-state, captures for evidence, read-only capability detection.

## Requires explicit task permission

Scene/prefab/GameObject mutation, script create/delete via tooling, menu execute, package install/upgrade, AssetGeneration, Play Mode control for demos, closing the Editor to run batch tests.

## Never do automatically

- Install/upgrade Unity packages (including Pipeline)
- Rewrite Cursor MCP / `unity mcp configure`
- Force-quit the user’s Editor
- Invoke arbitrary C# eval for routine inspect/mutate work
- Claim gameplay proof from tooling success or screenshots alone

## After mutations

- Read console for errors/warnings introduced by the change.
- Read back changed properties; confirm they match the approved target.
- For scene/prefab edits: inspect the **complete** serialized Git diff (incidental YAML included).
- If captures were requested: verify on-disk paths (CLI may remap into `Assets/`); prefer evidence outside `Assets/` when supported.
- Report: succeeded / failed / **not Play Mode–verified**.
- Distinguish Console inspection, visual observation (Scene View ≠ Main Camera), and actual gameplay interaction tests.
